Read `llms.txt` at the repository root before generating `.hmx` content — it is canonical
and lists the mistakes that are actually common.

The four that cause most failures:

1. Nesting containers needs MORE colons on the outer fence: `::::grid` wrapping `:::card`.
   Equal widths do not nest; the inner fence closes the outer container (`HMX1001`).
2. Interpolation is `{{ expr }}`. Single braces are ordinary text. Attribute values use
   `{key={expr}}`.
3. `@state`, `@if`, `@for` do not exist — rejected in ADR-0014. Everything is a directive:
   `::state{count=0}`.
4. Expressions cannot call functions and cannot reach globals. Assignment is legal only
   inside an event handler, only to declared state.

Verify generated documents with `hmx check <file>`. Exit code 0 means valid.

When changing the repository itself, read `AGENTS.md`.
